From: Wael Hasnaoui <24696530+Loukious@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] block: order timestamp flag clearing before plug detachment

blk_plug_invalidate_ts() assumes that PF_BLOCK_TS implies a non-NULL plug.
An arm64 AutoFDO build can inline __blk_flush_plug() and detach the plug
before clearing the flag. A preemption in that window makes the scheduler
write through a NULL pointer when the task resumes.

Keep the flag clear ordered before plug detachment with a compiler barrier.
This retains AutoFDO and requires no hardware memory fence.

The diagnosis, compiler experiments, patch, and changelog were prepared
with OpenAI Codex assistance.

Fixes: fad156c2af22 ("block: invalidate cached plug timestamp after task switch")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
---
diff --git a/block/blk-core.c b/block/blk-core.c
index c7f36c048..e64f5dbac 100644
--- a/block/blk-core.c
+++ b/block/blk-core.c
@@ -1295,6 +1295,12 @@ void blk_finish_plug(struct blk_plug *plug)
 {
 	if (plug == current->plug) {
 		__blk_flush_plug(plug, false);
+		/*
+		 * A preempted task invalidates its cached timestamp when it is
+		 * scheduled back in. Keep the PF_BLOCK_TS clear above ordered
+		 * before detaching the plug, including when the flush is inlined.
+		 */
+		barrier();
 		current->plug = NULL;
 	}
 }
